{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the goat shall bear upon it all their iniquities.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory interpreted (Beresheet Rabbah 65:15): 'עֲוֹנֹת תָּם — the iniquities of the blameless one — this is Jacob, a blameless man.' And it is fitting, for all who cause the many to sin — the sin of the many hangs upon him. And it is known that Samael always strives to cause Israel to sin, and likewise Esau-Edom — all their schemes are to cause Israel to sin, by force of the blessing 'וְהָיָה כַאֲשֶׁר תָּרִיד וּפָרַקְתָּ עֻלּוֹ' (Genesis 27:40). Therefore it is fitting to load upon him all the iniquities of the children of the blameless one, to say: Jacob, for his part, is blameless with HaShem, but you caused them to sin — therefore you shall bear their sin to Samael, the prince of Esau, who is called 'a hairy man.' And his dispatch to the land of Gezerah resembles exactly what is said (Joel 2:20): 'וְאֶת הַצְּפוֹנִי אַרְחִיק מֵעֲלֵיכֶם וְהִדַּחְתִּיו אֶל אֶרֶץ צִיָּה וּשְׁמָמָה.' 'And he shall send him by the hand of an appointed man' — our Sages of blessed memory said (cited in the Chizkuni on 16:21): this means that his time had arrived to die in that year."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The closing citation regarding 'an appointed man' (אִישׁ עִתִּי) refers to the Sages' reading of עִתִּי as 'one whose time has come'; the parenthetical (מובא בחזקוני טז כא) indicates the source is cited in the Chizkuni commentary on Leviticus 16:21."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:37:01.559666335Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}